<decompilertest>
<!--
  Authored SSE COMISS/COMISD probe: seta, setae, setbe and setb after a
  compare with a memory operand, a borrow (sbb) after COMISD, and a jbe
  branch after UCOMISS. Each condition flag is true for unordered inputs
  (ZF=PF=CF=1), so x > one must print as one < x (false for a NaN) and
  setbe as !(one < x) (true for a NaN), never as x <= one.
  P3 nanignore folding (kuna_floatnegation.rs) keeps the exact single
  comparison before the NaN guards are dropped. Strict correctness fix,
  no new option: pass 1 pins the defaults, pass 2 (nanignore none) keeps
  the explicit guards. The compiled-C oracle is in
  kuna-cli/tests/float_unordered_compare.rs.
-->
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
